00:03:20.095 --> 00:03:21.195
it makes total sense like-

00:03:21.585 --> 00:03:24.635
I- this is a thing I understand later cause it was

00:03:24.635 --> 00:03:27.645
so shocking to me, this revelation like- "I don't have any friends at all"

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:31.275
but I wish this was in the last video. This is the house I grew up in

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.880
This is the school I went to

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.545
it's called [something in swedish] it's where all the privileged

00:03:36.545 --> 00:03:39.325
kids went to school and I really appreciate my mom putting me in a

00:03:39.325 --> 00:03:42.335
really good school. Namaste mom. Even tho it did come

00:03:42.335 --> 00:03:44.945
with a price of not having any friends- umm

00:03:44.945 --> 00:03:47.495
I can't really see anything I don't know why I wanna look into the school

00:03:47.495 --> 00:03:50.575
like some goddamn creep but I don't remember much

00:03:50.585 --> 00:03:53.235
except one time there was a legendary snowball fight

00:03:53.235 --> 00:03:56.255
between two schools over here cause all

00:03:56.255 --> 00:03:59.075
the kids from this other school- they came over and

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.380
we had a legendary snowball fight over this fence [laughs]

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.955
LEGENDARY. It was like the battle

00:04:04.955 --> 00:04:08.055
of Normandy, basically. I remember

00:04:08.055 --> 00:04:10.785
we also used to call like- all the kids, all the other kids

00:04:10.785 --> 00:04:12.905
like "intruders" and we had to have

00:04:12.905 --> 00:04:15.935
this big meeting about not calling eachother intruders

00:04:15.935 --> 00:04:18.395
very swedish, very nice [laughs]

00:04:18.895 --> 00:04:21.845
I also remember someone pulling the fire alarm and we had to have a meeting too

00:04:21.845 --> 00:04:24.415
and then the principal- we were like

00:04:24.425 --> 00:04:27.545
it's four hundred people in the room and the principal stands up and

00:04:27.545 --> 00:04:30.725
be like "can the one that pulled the fire alarm

00:04:30.725 --> 00:04:33.575
PLEEEASE come forward"- and like, OBVIOUSLY THEY'RE NOT

00:04:33.575 --> 00:04:36.375
GONNA DO THAT in front of four hundred people like "yeah it was me,

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.285
I'm sorry"- it wasn't me by the way okay,

00:04:39.285 --> 00:04:41.135
IT WASN'T ME. There was also uh-

00:04:41.575 --> 00:04:44.325
I don't know for some reason this is where we entered the school

00:04:44.325 --> 00:04:47.335
and there was like a lady that you HAD to say hi to

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.140
I don't know why-  is that a swedish thing? I can't tell

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.095
She was nice. Don't get me wrong. Oh my God

00:04:53.095 --> 00:04:54.765
they still have these squares [laughs]

00:04:55.725 --> 00:04:57.855
I can't believe they still have these squares, God bless

00:04:58.165 --> 00:05:00.675
those squares were the best game ever, I don't know if you guys

00:05:00.675 --> 00:05:03.465
had these in school, but you had a basket ball

00:05:03.465 --> 00:05:06.555
and we called it king but it probably has some other name for you

00:05:06.555 --> 00:05:09.405
but basically, there was a king in one square

00:05:09.405 --> 00:05:12.035
and then there was a queen and then there 
were these two pawns

00:05:12.035 --> 00:05:14.325
and you started off as a pawn- and then

00:05:14.325 --> 00:05:17.325
if someone obviously gets out of the game you move up

00:05:17.325 --> 00:05:20.295
until you become the king, so basically the way you play

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.140
was that- the one that was king could make up the rules

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.540
of the game.[Laughs] So as soon as you become King

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:28.860
You're like "OK, the rules are X, Y, Z" like-

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.900
and you can just make up any rules whatsoever, which was idk

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.720
thats was just to made it fun. you could be like "ok I-

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:39.060
you lose if the ball bounces in your court" and then you just go *BLaAaA!* [Laughs]

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.960
And then a lot of times, what you would do is that you would come up

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.260
with a pack, with a queen so you would just work together to

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:48.140
eliminate everyone else, so no one else could beat you

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:51.020
which led to a lot of scumbaggery. I remembered like a lot

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:54.100
of bullying where you'd just target- I wasn't a bully ok

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.760
But we would target just like specific people and be like

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.560
"oh yeah, this person can't play" idk [giggles]

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:02.560
people get so upset of this ba- game, I remember the

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.900
people are leaving, going outside the school which wasn't allowed

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:09.000
just 'cause they get so mad over playing this game.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.120
Ah, So it makes me really happy the people still have these

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.520
Godawful game

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.440
